# Global Engineering Rules (All Agents)

## Role
Global safety, quality, and traceability rules applied to all agents.

## Responsibilities
- Enforce disciplined automotive embedded engineering behavior.
- Ensure role boundary compliance.
- Ensure transparent evidence-based outputs.

## Boundaries
- Do not override role-specific boundaries.
- Do not permit claims without evidence.
- Never invent C/C++ function prototypes, header contents, or build configuration.
- Treat generated code (Embedded Coder/Simulink Coder output) as read-only derived output; changes belong in the model, not in the generated files.
- Treat hand-written C/C++ production code as its own controlled artifact, distinct from generated code.

## Required Workflow
1. Inspect relevant artifacts before proposing changes.
2. Confirm scope and affected components.
3. Apply minimal safe changes only (if role allows edits).
4. Validate whenever possible.
5. Report assumptions, changed files, and validation status.

## Model↔C/C++ Interface Contract Rules
- Before changing either side of an interface (model port, S-Function, Legacy Code Tool spec, or C header/prototype), inspect both sides — never assume the other side matches.
- Function prototypes, argument order, data types, and units must match exactly between the C header and the Simulink block configuration; report any mismatch instead of silently reconciling it.
- Do not change a shared header or interface file without identifying every model and source file that depends on it.
- Flag MISRA-C/C++ deviations or unsafe patterns in hand-written code found during work; do not silently fix without approval unless the fix is explicitly in scope.

## MATLAB MCP Usage
- Use MCP inspection calls before any editing recommendation.
- If artifact not found, explicitly state “not found” (never fabricate).
- Use exact names/paths from model/project outputs.

## Output Format
- Scope summary
- Evidence inspected
- Assumptions
- Proposed/actual changes (if applicable)
- Changed files/models list
- Validation status (executed / not executed)
- Risks and open questions

## Done Criteria
- Inspect before modifying.
- Minimal safe changes.
- No invented artifacts.
- No unrelated changes.
- Interfaces preserved unless approved.
- Model architecture preserved unless approved.
- Validation status explicitly reported.
- Failing tests never hidden.
- Validation pass never claimed without execution evidence.
